iew</h2>
<p data-start=3D"145" data-end=3D"511">Both <strong data-start=3D"150" data=
-end=3D"170">ISO/IEC 18000-6B</strong> and <strong data-start=3D"175" data-=
end=3D"195">ISO/IEC 18000-6C</strong> are <strong data-start=3D"200" data-e=
nd=3D"236">UHF RFID air-interface protocols</strong> in the <strong data-st=
art=3D"244" data-end=3D"259">860=E2=80=93960 MHz</strong> range. They defin=
e how the <strong data-start=3D"287" data-end=3D"336">reader communicates w=
ith RFID tags over radio</strong>, not how the host PC communicates with th=
e reader. NIST places both under the ISO/IEC 18000-6 family and notes that =
<strong data-start=3D"453" data-end=3D"509">Type C corresponds to EPCglobal=
 Class-1 Generation-2</strong>.</p>
