<h3 data-section-id=3D"w7z9fq" data-start=3D"3795" data-end=3D"3830">What c=
hanges between 6B and 6C?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3831" data-end=3D"4134">The overall flow above is similar =
for both because both are interrogator-talks-first UHF RFID systems, but <s=
trong data-start=3D"3938" data-end=3D"4025">the signaling details, forward-=
channel encoding, and anti-collision behavior differ</strong> between 6B an=
d 6C. NIST explicitly notes these differences and states Type C is the Gen2=
-equivalent branch.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4136" data-end=3D"4139">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"1p5z311" data-start=3D"4141" data-end=3D"4161">7. Re=
commendation</h2>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"10khmb5" data-start=3D"4163" data-end=3D"4193"><span=
 role=3D"text">Choose <strong data-start=3D"4174" data-end=3D"4187">6C / Ge=
n2</strong> when:</span></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4194" data-end=3D"4308">
<li data-section-id=3D"177unke" data-start=3D"4194" data-end=3D"4219">
<p data-start=3D"4196" data-end=3D"4219">you are buying new tags</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"16z9gja" data-start=3D"4220" data-end=3D"4246">
<p data-start=3D"4222" data-end=3D"4246">you want easier sourcing</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1rx1qh1" data-start=3D"4247" data-end=3D"4275">
<p data-start=3D"4249" data-end=3D"4275">you need multi-tag reading</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"14xnsxf" data-start=3D"4276" data-end=3D"4308">
<p data-start=3D"4278" data-end=3D"4308">you are building a new system</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1wdeijo" data-start=3D"4310" data-end=3D"4337"><span=
 role=3D"text">Care about <strong data-start=3D"4325" data-end=3D"4331">6B<=
/strong> when:</span></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4338" data-end=3D"4469">
<li data-section-id=3D"13e4wsp" data-start=3D"4338" data-end=3D"4377">
<p data-start=3D"4340" data-end=3D"4377">you already have deployed legacy t=
ags</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1949smd" data-start=3D"4378" data-end=3D"4435">
<p data-start=3D"4380" data-end=3D"4435">an existing system specification e=
xplicitly requires 6B</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"v6rpr9" data-start=3D"4436" data-end=3D"4469">
<p data-start=3D"4438" data-end=3D"4469">backward compatibility matters</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4471" data-end=3D"4474">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"10gdpep" data-start=3D"4476" data-end=3D"4510">8. On=
e-Line Engineering Summary</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4512" data-end=3D"4655"><strong data-start=3D"4512" data-e=
nd=3D"4654">6B is mainly for legacy compatibility; 6C is the mainstream mod=
ern UHF RFID protocol and the better default for new HX-R01B-9 deployments.=
</strong></p>
