<h2 data-section-id=3D"1uen8oo" data-start=3D"3494" data-end=3D"3547">Is pu=
re software implementation on STM32 possible?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3549" data-end=3D"3907">In theory, with enough external RF=
 hardware and a lot of engineering effort, you could implement significant =
parts of the protocol on STM32 firmware. But in practice, for a commercial =
or even serious prototype system, that is <strong data-start=3D"3775" data-=
end=3D"3827">much harder than using a dedicated UHF reader IC</strong>. The=
 RF and timing requirements are the hard part, not the high-level firmware.=
</p>
<p data-start=3D"3909" data-end=3D"3933">So the honest answer is:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3935" data-end=3D"4166">
<li data-section-id=3D"xn4s5p" data-start=3D"3935" data-end=3D"4003">
<p data-start=3D"3937" data-end=3D"4003"><strong data-start=3D"3937" data-e=
nd=3D"3952">STM32 only:</strong> not realistically enough for a complete UH=
F reader</p>
