<p data-start=3D"4006" data-end=3D"4063"><strong data-start=3D"4006" data-e=
nd=3D"4044">STM32 + dedicated UHF reader chip:</strong> yes, very feasible<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"185wlf8" data-start=3D"4064" data-end=3D"4083">
<p data-start=3D"4066" data-end=3D"4083"><strong data-start=3D"4066" data-e=
nd=3D"4073">6C:</strong> practical</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"64cy1g" data-start=3D"4084" data-end=3D"4166">
<p data-start=3D"4086" data-end=3D"4166"><strong data-start=3D"4086" data-e=
nd=3D"4093">6B:</strong> possible, but more custom work depending on the RF=
 chip and mode support</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-section-id=3D"1ayo5sc" data-start=3D"4168" data-end=3D"4185">Recom=
mendation</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4187" data-end=3D"4281">If you want to build something lik=
e <strong data-start=3D"4223" data-end=3D"4236">HX-R01B-9</strong> or a sma=
ller embedded UHF reader with STM32:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4283" data-end=3D"4473">
<li data-section-id=3D"q2sv60" data-start=3D"4283" data-end=3D"4323">
<p data-start=3D"4285" data-end=3D"4323">choose an <strong data-start=3D"42=
95" data-end=3D"4304">STM32</strong> for system control</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1mvixm3" data-start=3D"4324" data-end=3D"4383">
<p data-start=3D"4326" data-end=3D"4383">pair it with a <strong data-start=
=3D"4341" data-end=3D"4383">dedicated UHF RFID reader IC/front end</strong>=
</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1pbydj9" data-start=3D"4384" data-end=3D"4416">
<p data-start=3D"4386" data-end=3D"4416">prioritize <strong data-start=3D"4=
397" data-end=3D"4416">18000-6C / Gen2</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"qdxpte" data-start=3D"4417" data-end=3D"4473">
<p data-start=3D"4419" data-end=3D"4473">only add <strong data-start=3D"442=
