<h2 data-section-id=3D"1ai91g4" data-start=3D"3867" data-end=3D"3890">What =
each block does</h2>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1lobewi" data-start=3D"3892" data-end=3D"3909">UHF R=
eader IC</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3910" data-end=3D"4143">Handles the RFID protocol side: mo=
dulation, demodulation, framing, CRC, and inventory logic support. A reader=
 IC in the <strong data-start=3D"4030" data-end=3D"4050">ST25RU3993 class</=
strong> is designed for the <strong data-start=3D"4071" data-end=3D"4086">8=
40=E2=80=93960 MHz</strong> UHF RFID band and supports Gen2-class reader fu=
nctions.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"lpe6we" data-start=3D"4145" data-end=3D"4165">Matchi=
ng / Balun</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4166" data-end=3D"4267">Converts the reader IC RF interfac=
e to a <strong data-start=3D"4207" data-end=3D"4237">50 =CE=A9 single-ended=
 RF chain</strong> and helps tune the front end.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"p87lkr" data-start=3D"4269" data-end=3D"4293">Driver=
 / External PA</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4294" data-end=3D"4470">Boosts transmit power so the reade=
r can energize passive tags at longer range. ST=E2=80=99s high-power reader=
 reference uses an <strong data-start=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4429">external P=
A</strong> for higher output fixed-reader designs.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"ozt1r5" data-start=3D"4472" data-end=3D"4503">Harmon=
ic / Band-pass filter</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4504" data-end=3D"4581">Suppresses unwanted emissions and =
helps keep the output clean for compliance.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"gjnae6" data-start=3D"4583" data-end=3D"4618">Direct=
ional coupler + detectors</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4619" data-end=3D"4725">Measures <strong data-start=3D"462=
8" data-end=3D"4639">forward</strong> and <strong data-start=3D"4644" data-=
end=3D"4657">reflected</strong> power so you can monitor mismatch, antenna =
tuning, and PA behavior.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"x2phqh" data-start=3D"4727" data-end=3D"4751">RF swi=
tch / T-R path</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4752" data-end=3D"4853">Routes the antenna path and helps =
isolate the sensitive receive side from the stronger transmit path.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"tsvtml" data-start=3D"4855" data-end=3D"4892">Leakag=
e cancellation / protection</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4893" data-end=3D"5021">Reduces self-jamming caused by TX =
leakage into the RX path. This is one of the most important blocks in long-=
range RFID readers.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"s1bwl7" data-start=3D"5023" data-end=3D"5060">Antenn=
a matching + reader antenna</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5061" data-end=3D"5217">Final tuning stage into the actual=
 <strong data-start=3D"5096" data-end=3D"5119">865=E2=80=93868 MHz antenna<=
/strong>. For long-range fixed readers, a <strong data-start=3D"5153" data-=
end=3D"5188">directional patch/panel antenna</strong> is the usual starting=
 point.</p>
