<h3 data-section-id=3D"11dkagn" data-start=3D"4432" data-end=3D"4461">What =
it does electrically</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4462" data-end=3D"4734">The PA takes a relatively small RF=
 drive signal and increases its power while preserving the modulation envel=
ope enough for the tag to decode commands correctly. In RFID, linearity sti=
ll matters, but not in the same way as in wideband communications; what mat=
ters most is:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4735" data-end=3D"4890">
<li data-section-id=3D"xh5r7m" data-start=3D"4735" data-end=3D"4759">
<p data-start=3D"4737" data-end=3D"4759">clean modulation depth</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"p8u4ra" data-start=3D"4760" data-end=3D"4791">
<p data-start=3D"4762" data-end=3D"4791">controlled spectral emissions</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1dmsjxy" data-start=3D"4792" data-end=3D"4822">
<p data-start=3D"4794" data-end=3D"4822">stable output under mismatch</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"546gi7" data-start=3D"4823" data-end=3D"4841">
<p data-start=3D"4825" data-end=3D"4841">thermal behavior</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1xk2itu" data-start=3D"4842" data-end=3D"4890">
<p data-start=3D"4844" data-end=3D"4890">not desensitizing the receive path=
 excessively</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"wgwuyd" data-start=3D"4892" data-end=3D"4910">Why it=
 matters</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4911" data-end=3D"4939">This block strongly affects:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4940" data-end=3D"5054">
<li data-section-id=3D"sv27hb" data-start=3D"4940" data-end=3D"4963">
<p data-start=3D"4942" data-end=3D"4963">achievable read range</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"qxcl0r" data-start=3D"4964" data-end=3D"4983">
<p data-start=3D"4966" data-end=3D"4983">compliance margin</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"kqdcl2" data-start=3D"4984" data-end=3D"5001">
<p data-start=3D"4986" data-end=3D"5001">heat generation</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"kxdjoc" data-start=3D"5002" data-end=3D"5020">
<p data-start=3D"5004" data-end=3D"5020">harmonic content</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"wj4l2l" data-start=3D"5021" data-end=3D"5054">
<p data-start=3D"5023" data-end=3D"5054">required filtering after the PA</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5056" data-end=3D"5384">For EU 865=E2=80=93868 MHz, PA pow=
er cannot be chosen in isolation; it must be considered with antenna gain s=
o the final system remains within the applicable regional constraints. RAIN=
=E2=80=99s design guideline explicitly discusses EIRP and how antenna gain =
factors into the allowed radiated power budget. <span class=3D"" data-state=
=3D"closed"><span class=3D"ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center select-=
