<h3 data-section-id=3D"11dkagn" data-start=3D"5754" data-end=3D"5783">What =
it does electrically</h3>
<p data-start=3D"5784" data-end=3D"5859">After amplification, the signal al=
ways contains unwanted spectral products:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5860" data-end=3D"5972">
<li data-section-id=3D"11dcreu" data-start=3D"5860" data-end=3D"5889">
<p data-start=3D"5862" data-end=3D"5889">harmonics from nonlinearity</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1u9b0fr" data-start=3D"5890" data-end=3D"5911">
<p data-start=3D"5892" data-end=3D"5911">switching artifacts</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1eby6pq" data-start=3D"5912" data-end=3D"5972">
<p data-start=3D"5914" data-end=3D"5972">spurious products from the synthes=
izer or modulation edges</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5974" data-end=3D"6029">A filter suppresses these undesire=
d components so that:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6030" data-end=3D"6216">
<li data-section-id=3D"1jj0fb1" data-start=3D"6030" data-end=3D"6067">
<p data-start=3D"6032" data-end=3D"6067">the transmitted spectrum is cleane=
r</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1cf5xa" data-start=3D"6068" data-end=3D"6101">
<p data-start=3D"6070" data-end=3D"6101">regulatory compliance is easier</p=
>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"j4eu8z" data-start=3D"6102" data-end=3D"6160">
<p data-start=3D"6104" data-end=3D"6160">the antenna does not radiate too m=
uch out-of-band energy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1m0nr2s" data-start=3D"6161" data-end=3D"6216">
<p data-start=3D"6163" data-end=3D"6216">the detector/coupler measurements =
are more meaningful</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"wgwuyd" data-start=3D"6218" data-end=3D"6236">Why it=
 matters</h3>
<p data-start=3D"6237" data-end=3D"6262">Without proper filtering:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6263" data-end=3D"6454">
<li data-section-id=3D"mk1yvi" data-start=3D"6263" data-end=3D"6295">
<p data-start=3D"6265" data-end=3D"6295">compliance failures are likely</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"16feirm" data-start=3D"6296" data-end=3D"6328">
<p data-start=3D"6298" data-end=3D"6328">harmonics can radiate strongly</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"13o7syk" data-start=3D"6329" data-end=3D"6383">
<p data-start=3D"6331" data-end=3D"6383">reflected-power measurements becom=
e less trustworthy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1v437te" data-start=3D"6384" data-end=3D"6454">
<p data-start=3D"6386" data-end=3D"6454">the receive path may suffer more i=
n-band and near-band contamination</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6456" data-end=3D"6626">For a single-region EU design, a f=
ilter optimized around <strong data-start=3D"6513" data-end=3D"6528">865=E2=
=80=93868 MHz</strong> is much easier to realize than a wideband global fro=
nt end. <span class=3D"" data-state=3D"closed"><span class=3D"ms-1 inline-f=
