<h1 data-section-id=3D"1owyd8g" data-start=3D"6633" data-end=3D"6657">5) Di=
rectional Coupler</h1>
<p data-start=3D"6659" data-end=3D"7146">This is one of the most important =
RF blocks in a long-range reader. In ST=E2=80=99s high-power reference, a <=
strong data-start=3D"6759" data-end=3D"6788">20 dB directional coupler</str=
ong> first samples a small amount of TX power for a detector, and then a <s=
trong data-start=3D"6857" data-end=3D"6891">main 10 dB directional coupler<=
/strong> acts as the directional unit that isolates the transmit path from =
the receive path. ST explicitly says this main coupler plays a <strong data=
-start=3D"7021" data-end=3D"7044">very important role</strong> because its =
parasitics strongly influence reader sensitivity. <span class=3D"" data-sta=
