<h1 data-section-id=3D"1lcuxb0" data-start=3D"14019" data-end=3D"14070">11)=
 Carrier Cancellation / Leakage Cancellation</h1>
<p data-start=3D"14071" data-end=3D"14193">Your generated image does not sh=
ow this block explicitly, but it is important enough that it should be in t=
he real design.</p>
<p data-start=3D"14195" data-end=3D"14769">ST=E2=80=99s reference design us=
es a <strong data-start=3D"14224" data-end=3D"14256">carrier cancellation c=
ircuit</strong> connected to the <strong data-start=3D"14274" data-end=3D"1=
4290">coupled port</strong> of the main directional coupler. Its job is to =
reflect a controlled amount of sampled carrier back into the coupler so tha=
t it cancels the <strong data-start=3D"14430" data-end=3D"14446">self-jammi=
ng</strong> signal at the isolated port before the signal enters the receiv=
er. ST explains that if the reflected cancellation signal has the same ampl=
itude and opposite phase as the self-jammer, they cancel. The circuit uses =
<strong data-start=3D"14660" data-end=3D"14696">three digital tunable capac=
itors</strong> under <strong data-start=3D"14703" data-end=3D"14728">STM32 =
control via SPI</strong>. <span class=3D"" data-state=3D"closed"><span clas=
s=3D"ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center select-none relative top-[-0.=
